        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Colin Thiele\n- Places: Thiele Highway, Bower, South Australia, Western Australia, Victoria, New South Wales\n- Roles: author, educator\n- Topics: South Australia, Australian literature, species distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Colin Milton Thiele was born on 16 November 1920 and died on 4 September 2006.\n- Colin Milton Thiele was an Australian author and educator.\n- Thiele Highway is named after Colin Thiele.\n- Colin Thiele lived most of his life in towns along the route of Thiele Highway and set some of his stories in that area.\n- Bower is a town in South Australia located approximately halfway between Eudunda and Morgan on the Thiele Highway.\n- Bossiaea walkeri occurs in Western Australia, South Australia, Victoria, and New South Wales.",
